# Godot generated data
.godot/
*.uid

# .import files are NOT generated data, whatever the name suggests: they hold the per-asset import
# SETTINGS, and losing them silently re-imports every asset on defaults. That is not theoretical
# here — the terrain control map has to import lossless, because VRAM compression bleeds its three
# channels into each other, and both character GLBs import through a humanoid BoneMap without which
# neither rig is retargeted. Godot's own template does not ignore them either.

# Local/editor settings
.idea/
.vscode/

# Generated renders, captures and local test output
renders/
captures/
logs/
user://
*.log

# Imported previews generated from removed laboratory assets
assets/models/animations/ogre_baked_before/glb/*.png

# OS files
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
